            <ArticleTitle>Control of postoperative pain by interactive demand analgesia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>385-91</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A demand analgesia apparatus is described. It communicates with the patient by means of spoken messages in any desired language, so that preliminary instruction is unnecessary. Dosage is limited by a reduction in respiratory rate, and by a series of electronic fail-safe circuits. Operation of the system is illustrated in a series of 10 patients given fentanyl &quot;on demand&quot; for the first 12 h after operation. The mean dose rate 0.73 +/- 0.49 microgram min-1. There was no evidence of cumulation or tolerance during the period of study.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
